    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0176" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 832.73/143</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul in Charge at Rio de Janeiro</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Momsen</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1249</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 25, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to despatch No. 1068 of December
                    17, 1917,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d68-f1"/> from this Consulate General, I have the
                    honor to report that there was <pb facs="0177" n="65" xml:id="pg65"/> published
                    in the <hi rendition="#italic">Diario Official</hi> (Official Gazette) of March
                    14, 1918, an order of the Minister of Transportation and Public Works— <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush">granting to Mr. Nelson O’Shaughnessy, representative
                            of the Western Union Telegraph Co., for the company or for any other
                            company which may be organized, permission, without monopoly or special
                            privilege of any kind, to lay and operate two submarine cables from the
                            city of Nictheroy (which is the capital of the State of Rio de Janeiro,
                            and situated directly across the bay from this city): one with landing
                            places on the island of Itaparica, the city of Aracajú, the island of
                            Fernando de Noronha, the cities of Parahyba, Natal and Belem, and from
                            there to the Greater Antilles; and another from Nictheroy to the city of
                            Paranagua, to be connected with Maldonado in the Republic of Uruguay,
                            with permission to be prolonged to the Republic Argentina.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. P. Momsen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
